  {
   "id": 241277,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "What was the Plague of Athens? Compare the summaries below and select the one that best describes this disease and correctly identifies related current impacts.",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 754570,
     "content_html": "The Plague of Athens was a disease believed caused by <i>Yersinia pestis</i> that killed one-quarter of Athenian troops in 430 BC. The bacterium causes between 10 and 15 million cases of typhoid fever today, resulting in over 10,000 deaths annually."
    },
    {
     "id": 754569,
     "content_html": "The Plague of Athens was a disease believed caused by Salmonella entericaserovar <i>typhi</i> that killed one-quarter of Athenian troops in 430 BC. The bacterium causes between 5 and 10 million cases of typhoid fever today, resulting in over 20,000 deaths annually."
    },
    {
     "id": 754568,
     "content_html": "The Plague of Athens was a disease believed caused by <i>Yersinia pestis</i> that killed one-quarter of Athenian troops in 430 BC. The bacterium causes between 16 and 33 million cases of typhoid fever today, resulting in over 200,000 deaths annually."
    },
    {
     "id": 754571,
     "content_html": "The Plague of Athens was a disease believed caused by Salmonella entericaserovar <i>typhi</i> that killed one-quarter of Athenian troops in 430 BC. The bacterium causes between 16 and 33 million cases of typhoid fever today, resulting in over 200,000 deaths annually."
